    "layout_review": "The final root and standalone documents have 43 article pages and 17 supplement pages, with clean pdfLaTeX logs. Article pages 1-3 and 20-43 and supplement pages 16-17 were rendered and inspected after the twenty-five-pentagon adoption; no blocking clipping, overlap or formula issue was found.",
    "naming_style": "Removed 36 visible square-bracket titles from theorem-like environments; retained all internal labels and references, and converted the four protected-pentagon local facts to Claims 1-4.",
    "review_2026_10_14": "Article revision: relative pentagon restoration maps along a bottom Hamilton path. On 2026-10-15 the relative-normalization replay was added to verify_protected_pentagons.py; certificate source and supplement PDF unchanged; all suites re-run with verify_all.py --write-reports.",
    "revision_2026_10_16": "Extended the Hamiltonian subclass from at most seven to at most nine distinct 5-cycles using shared-hub path reductions of orders four and five. Added supplement Appendix E, the two literal cycle-family files, an exact reader and six negative cases; preserved the historical literal blocks and the general open bounds [4,5].",
    "revision_2026_10_16_eleven": "Extended the Hamiltonian subclass from at most nine to at most eleven distinct 5-cycles using seven further local reductions and the existing subcubic theorem. Added supplement Appendix F, seven unchanged literal witness families, two exact readers, two reports and sixteen negative cases. Preserved the 56 preceding marked certificate blocks, earlier local readers and earlier JSON witnesses; the general open bounds remain [4,5].",
    "revision_2026_10_16_pentagonal_reservoirs": "Extended the Hamiltonian subclass to at most fifteen distinct 5-cycles, added the unbounded one-heavy-vertex class and two-degenerate classes with at most three heavy vertices or seventeen 5-cycles. Added Appendix G, three unchanged component-cycle witnesses, two independent readers, two reports and twenty-two negative cases. Preserved 57 earlier marked blocks, six local readers and nine earlier JSON witnesses. The unrestricted thresholds remain [4,5]; any vertex-minimal counterexample has at least sixteen distinct 5-cycles.",
    "revision_2026_10_16_twenty_five": "Adopted the twenty-five-pentagon, six-heavy-vertex and two-degenerate seven-heavy-vertex theorems, with connected-cycle and bowtie restorations. Added Appendices H-I, ten unchanged literal inputs, five Python files, four positive reports and forty-four negative cases. All 58 preceding marked blocks, eight local readers, twelve literal inputs and 53 earlier rejection records are preserved. The paired 558 clique trees support both product families; the path partitions for the older 2982 boundary templates and redundant order-ten path remain external audit evidence. All seven original suites and manifests passed with byte-identical reports; arbitrary-order proofs remain analytic and the unrestricted thresholds remain [4,5].",
